---
// PLACEHOLDER content — owner: search this file for "PLACEHOLDER" and verify each value.
import Guest from '../../layouts/Guest.astro';
---
<Guest title="TV & Streaming">
  <p>Access your favorite shows and movies during your stay.</p>

  <h2>TV Locations</h2>
  <ul>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li><strong>Living room:</strong> 65-inch Samsung smart TV</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li><strong>Primary bedroom:</strong> 50-inch TCL Roku smart TV</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Quick Start</h2>

  <h3>Turning On</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Press power on the main TV remote</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>TV should switch to HDMI 1 automatically</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>If not, press "Input" or "Source" and select Roku / HDMI 1</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Streaming Apps</h2>

  <p>Sign in with your own account, then sign out before checkout.</p>

  <h3>Pre-installed</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Netflix</li>
    <li>Hulu</li>
    <li>Disney+</li>
    <li>Amazon Prime Video</li>
    <li>HBO Max</li>
    <li>Apple TV+</li>
    <li>YouTube / YouTube TV</li>
    <li>Spotify</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="g-callout">
    <p><strong>Before you leave:</strong> sign out of every streaming account you signed into. Even one forgotten Netflix login is a privacy issue for the next guest.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound</h2>

  <h3>Soundbar</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Connected to the main TV</li>
    <li>Volume from the TV remote</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Bluetooth Pairing</h3>
  <ol>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Press and hold the Bluetooth button on the soundbar for 3 seconds</li>
    <li>Open Bluetooth on your phone</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Select "PinePrairie-Soundbar"</li>
    <li>Disconnect before you leave</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Screen Mirroring</h2>

  <h3>iPhone / iPad (AirPlay)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Same WiFi network as the TV</li>
    <li>Swipe down to Control Center → Screen Mirroring</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Select "PinePrairie Living Room TV"</li>
    <li>Enter code if prompted</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Android (Chromecast)</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Same WiFi network as the TV</li>
    <li>Open the app you want to cast from</li>
    <li>Tap the cast icon</li>
    <li>Select the TV from the list</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

  <h3>"No Signal" on screen</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Press "Input" or "Source" on the remote</li>
    <li>Select the correct HDMI input</li>
    <li>Ensure the streaming device is on</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Remote not working</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Check batteries</li>
    <li>Point directly at the TV</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Backup remote is in the living room media cabinet drawer</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>App not loading</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Close and reopen the app</li>
    <li>Check WiFi connection</li>
    <li>Restart the streaming device (unplug for 30 seconds)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before You Leave</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sign out of all streaming accounts</strong></li>
    <li>Disconnect Bluetooth devices</li>
    <li>Turn off all TVs and devices</li>
  </ul>

  <p style="margin-top: 32px;">Need help? See <a href="/guest/contacts">Contacts</a>.</p>
</Guest>
